<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Old Quarter</span>
<h1>Old Quarter by Motorbike: Motorbike Parking Guide in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Parking, more than riding, decides whether a motorbike day in the Hanoi Old Quarter feels easy or endless. The district’s lanes are narrow and shared, its curbs fill early, and every stop on your itinerary begins with the same small question: where does the bike go? This guide answers it the honest way, with the habits riders actually follow, the constraints that shape every decision, and the questions to check locally, rather than with invented rules or guaranteed spots.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">motorbike rental in the Hanoi Old Quarter</a> hub, sits alongside the wider <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource, and pairs with the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding skills. The rental itself is verified and fixed: Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, across the river from the Old Quarter, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00, and everything between pickup and return is what this guide helps you plan.</p>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
<p>On this page</p>
